    "q-65130": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65130",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ evaluate ${f}_{yxx}(1,1)$ if ${f}_{xy}(x,y)=y{e}^{xy}(2+xy).$",
      "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y) & ={f}_{xyx}(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy}(2+xy)) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}(2+xy)+{y}^{2}{e}^{xy} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}(3+xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{yxx}(1,1)=(1)^{2}{e}^{1\\cdot 1}(3+(1)(1))=4e\\,\\,\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
