    "q-133382": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133382",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Suppose that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}=\\frac{x{e}^{yz}}{x+y},\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}=-\\frac{z{e}^{yz}}{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate the following expression at the point $(1,1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂x∂y}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nHence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂y∂x∂y} & =\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x{e}^{yz}}{x+y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{yz}\\cdot (\\frac{1\\cdot (x+y)-x\\cdot 1}{(x+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{yz}}{(x+y)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn addition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-\\frac{z{e}^{yz}}{x+y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot ({e}^{yz}+yz{e}^{yz}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{yz}(1+yz)}{x+y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate both partial derivatives at the point $(1,1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =\\frac{1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}}{(1+1)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =-\\frac{{e}^{1\\cdot 0}(1+1\\cdot 0)}{1+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂x∂y∂x}{|}_{(1,1,0)}+\\frac{{∂}^{3}f}{∂z∂x∂z}{|}_{(1,1,0)} & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
